                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The crab-with-a-boomerang premise is charming and genuinely unique, but the execution drags it down. Controls initially shipped without a proper scheme and reportedly only got fixed after players emailed the publisher directly, and even now the aiming feels a bit off, forcing constant repositioning during fights; controls also can't be rebound. The crab's slow movement speed compounds the bigger issue: a lot of fetch-quest backtracking across screens with no map and few in-game hints, which turns exploration into tedious repetition rather than discovery. There's also a reported boss-fight bug on island 2 where the boss's health bar drains instantly before the fight even really starts, cutting the encounter short. Tightening the pacing (faster movement or shorter backtracks), adding a map, and fixing the boss health bug would go a long way toward letting the game's fun, weird concept shine through.",
